{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Your calf, Samaria, is cast off</b> — doubled, as if written אותך זנח עגלך / אותך שומרין (it has cast off your calf; it has rejected you, Samaria) — as though it said: it has rejected you, for the city will be destroyed and its people will go into exile." "<b>My anger has burned against them</b> — against the calf and against Samaria." "<b>Until when</b> — will My wrath burn against them, until they are cleansed." "<b>And they cannot be clean</b> — that they should have cleansing from it."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The commentary reads שומרון at the lemma head but שומרין in the body quotation; retained both forms as they appear."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:37.291270731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}